# (client/MANIFEST.md "Visual effects", "Spell colour light (O205)") does the rest. A magic effect that plays on the map
# lights the tiles around it for about 320 ms in a colour that matches it, so spells glow in caves and at night.
#  * Map keeps a table effect id -> {8-bit light colour, radius} (g_map.setSpellLightColor, sent by the module from
#    visualfx_logic.lua), the limits (g_map.setSpellLightConfig(enabled, max, ms, attack, minGap, minFade)) and the live
#    lights (at most `max`, 12 as shipped; a new effect finds the table full -> no light).
#  * Tile::addThing (the effect branch of 0116) calls Map::spellLightEffect(position, effectId); an unknown effect, the
#    option off, the same effect on the same tile again inside minGap ms, or a full table add nothing. No Lua callback.
#  * MapView::drawFloor adds the live lights of the camera floor to the map light view (the same addLight call the loot beam
#    pools of 0069 use) before the light section, strength rising over `attack` of the life and then falling smoothly; the
#    colour levels (each of red, green, blue 0..5 of the 8-bit colour) and the radius scale with it (visualfx_logic.lua
#    L.fade / L.dim / L.radiusAt are the same maths and are unit tested). The light view only adds light, so the surface in
#    full ambient light does not get brighter; with "Show light effects" off there is no light view and nothing is drawn.
#  * Option spellLight (default on), Options > Graphics under the other four visual effects of 0126.
# Not built or run: the hunks were written against the context lines of 0069, 0116 and 0126 (the base tree is not in git);
# every context line of a hunk was checked to occur in those patches (client/BASE.md 0127); the line numbers are approximate.
